== Thresholds implied by the fixed constants (exact integer arithmetic) ==
  u_0 = floor(eps*lambda) >= 1 needs lambda >= 131072 = 2^17, i.e. s > 2^131071
  (D.5) u_0 >= lambda^(4/5) needs lambda >= eps^-5 = 2^85 = 38685626227668133590597632, i.e. s > 2^(2^85 - 1)
  (D.5) D_arr = r^(2a) = 2^(12a) <= s^(1/1000): with a <= 4 eps lambda the exponent ratio is 48/131072 = 0.000366 <= 1/1000: holds for all s once a <= 4 eps lambda (note r^(2a), not r*2^a)
  depth: H < C s 8^-d  <=>  8^d < C floor(sqrt(lambda))  <=>  d < log2(lambda)/6 + log2(C)/3  (consistent)
  Lemma D.3 child size: 6M/r with r = 64 is 6/64 = 3/32 = 0.09375 < 1/8 = 0.12500: consistent
  at lambda = 2^17: u_0 = 1, a_0 = 2, L = 4, D_arr = 16777216 = 2^24, 2 D_arr^2 Delta = 2^49 * s^0.9; H ~ s/362; (D.6) M >= 2 D_arr^2 Delta needs s^0.1 >= 2^49 * 362, i.e. s >= 2^575: fine at s ~ 2^131072
